00:24:53,120 --> 00:25:05,680
And again, this goes back, David, to what I was talking about where you have to really think about Google and all the different inventory, like all the different traffic sources it serves on in comparison to some of the, you know, the other players.

263
00:25:06,320 --> 00:25:24,160
So one reason why you might see Google with like zero conversions in your MMP deterministic conversions or just a fraction of what Google is reporting or what scan reports is deterministic conversions can still happen if you're able to collect the user's IDFA, right?

264
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:40,400
But again, remember, so much of Google's traffic happens on browsers, on like websites, and the opportunity to collect user consent, the ATT prompt, right, does not exist on browsers.

265
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:43,440
And so I think people really overlooked that.

266
00:25:43,600 --> 00:25:53,520
And then probably the biggest one, and again, this is one of those things that I was talking about where I wish Google had been more vocal about it is that they did not prompt for it on YouTube.

