00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:17,520
How much do I need to spend?

289
00:27:17,840 --> 00:27:26,720
One of the things we didn't mention earlier is that it does sometimes take longer for UAC to, for the algorithm to get trained.

290
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:29,200
So sometimes it does take higher budget.

291
00:27:29,360 --> 00:27:31,440
But yeah, what are your thoughts on like getting started?

292
00:27:31,760 --> 00:27:32,720
I'll be consistent here.

293
00:27:32,880 --> 00:27:34,000
I've said it somewhere else.

294
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:37,920
I know people come at me and say, like,, well, that didn't work for me.

295
00:27:38,240 --> 00:27:40,480
And or like, do I really need to spend that much?

296
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:44,000
I'm going to use this as if you're starting in the US, okay?

297
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:48,400
Because if we're talking about other countries, then that becomes much more complicated.

298
00:27:48,720 --> 00:27:58,480
But in the US on Android, if you're saying, like, what is the minimum budget I need to start testing things, I would say anywhere from like 200 to 300 dollars a day.

299
00:27:59,040 --> 00:28:01,520
Yes, you could do less and sure you can do more.

300
00:28:01,840 --> 00:28:16,320
But like if I were to say, okay, you're just starting out, that's what I would probably want to spend on a daily basis to get enough information to get it fast enough to actually be able to say, okay, is, is this working or what adjustments do I need to make on iOS?

301
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:18,880
It's got to be more significant than that.

302
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:20,720
But it's also a more expensive platform.

303
00:28:21,360 --> 00:28:25,440
Installs are much more expensive on iOS than they are on Android.

304
00:28:25,840 --> 00:28:27,200
The inventory is more expensive.

305
00:28:27,360 --> 00:28:28,480
The CPMs are higher.

