00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:30,000
Like if you're spending $500 a day, how long is it going to take before the algorithm really figures out where to show your ads, how to show your ads?

342
00:31:30,800 --> 00:31:32,560
Any other tips on kind of ramping up?

343
00:31:33,120 --> 00:31:38,800
Usually within like two to three weeks, you can start to see how things are going to likely trend.

344
00:31:39,600 --> 00:31:46,400
One other thing that I notice as like a mistake that a lot of people do is they build out their campaigns as the bare minimum.

345
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:48,640
So they will create one campaign.

346
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:50,720
and then they'll have one ad group.

347
00:31:51,040 --> 00:31:54,960
And the ad group is, if you're familiar with Meta, is like an ad set, right?

348
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:58,720
And it's sort of a grouping of creative that you're testing.

349
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:04,480
Now, you can't assign budgets at the ad group level in Google, okay?

350
00:32:04,800 --> 00:32:16,480
So Google's just going to make the call and say, okay, we're going to send eighty percent of our traffic to this one ad group and ten percent to this other one and five to the last one, et cetera.

351
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:18,320
So you have no control over that.

352
00:32:18,880 --> 00:32:29,120
But what I always encourage people to do is you have to build out multiple ad groups and I like theme them., you know, think about use cases and/or features of your app.

353
00:32:29,520 --> 00:32:34,240
And then that's what I would create your ad groups around and see what kind of engagement you're getting on those.

354
00:32:34,560 --> 00:32:39,280
So if you have a I'm just going to use like a golf app, maybe it's swing performance.

355
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:40,800
That's one ad group.

356
00:32:41,360 --> 00:32:44,720
And then the next one is like about caddies.

357
00:32:45,280 --> 00:32:46,000
That's your next one.

358
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:50,240
And all your creative should somehow correspond to that central theme.

359
00:32:50,640 --> 00:32:53,040
And then you can see what people are interacting with.

360
00:32:53,200 --> 00:33:03,840
And I usually like to build out maybe about five ad groups per campaign, get a little bit traction, see what's resonating with folks as opposed to just doing one if it doesn't work.

361
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:06,000
And then you're like, well, I tried, right?

362
00:33:06,240 --> 00:33:07,440
It was like, no, you didn't.

