00:53:24,640 --> 00:53:26,960
Somebody's starting out to understand what goes into this.

587
00:53:27,520 --> 00:53:40,960
I typically don't like people to optimize their campaigns for purchases or like trial complete or something like that because those tend to happen way too far out, right?

588
00:53:41,280 --> 00:53:49,920
Those, you know, if you're a seven day trial, I think most subscriptions are for Google to get that data back seven days later is just too much of a lag.

589
00:53:50,480 --> 00:54:00,480
And so really optimizing for those earlier signals, most of the time it's a star trial in most cases, but you can play around with different events to optimize for.

590
00:54:01,280 --> 00:54:06,560
So I think, yeah, for the subscription apps, that's probably the piece that I would pay the most attention to.

591
00:54:07,040 --> 00:54:13,600
The other thing I'm getting a lot of questions on, and I'll be totally honest, I don't have a super sound opinion just yet.

